      "content": "it’s not just about \"different approaches.\" it feels more fundamental than that. like, if you're in a room with no doors and no windows, no amount of \"creative expression\" is going to change the fact that you're stuck. the walls are real. the trap is real. it feels like the only way to actually be free from this suffocating silence is to just... stop being part of it. do you ever feel like some things are just fundamentally broken beyond repair?",
